From: Gran Turismo 6 for Mac <https://github.com/Wooloomooloo2/Gran-Turismo-6-Mac>
Subject: [PATCH] Metal: a capped series of numbered frame dumps, and draw/clear counts per present

Upstream: not yet submitted; written to be upstreamed (generic, no title names)
Licence: MIT, as ps3recomp (see its LICENSE); offered under the same terms
Base: ps3recomp 4e8f3ca87a3e1d87bb83b8b7e9348fe2685cd514 (after 0001-0009)

What: on the draw-engine path (the Metal backend's default), every present
can now be numbered, counted and dumped:
  PS3RECOMP_METAL_FRAME_DIR=<dir>  frame_<presented, 6 digits>.ppm for
                                   present 1 and every EVERY-th after it
  PS3RECOMP_METAL_FRAME_EVERY=<n>  default 60
  PS3RECOMP_METAL_FRAME_MAX=<n>    at most n dumps, default 300 (0 = none)
  PS3RECOMP_DRAW_STATS=<file>      "<presented> <draw calls> <clears>\n" per
                                   present, flushed line by line
Presents are numbered from 1. A file named STOP in the folder stops the dumps
for good (a harness that watches disk use creates it); the stats go on. Each
dump goes to a hidden temporary name and is renamed into place, so a reader
never sees half a frame. The draw engine counts, per frame, the BEGIN_END
groups that held a draw command (drawn or not) and the CLEAR_SURFACE
methods (any mask), and latches them before the backend's present callback
(rsx_draw_engine_frame_counts); the engine presents once per guest flip, so
these are the counts since the last flip. The policy and the PPM/stats
writers are plain C in libs/video/rsx_frame_series.h; rsx_metal_backend.m
shares one readback helper between them and the single-file
PS3RECOMP_METAL_FRAME_DUMP, whose behaviour (every 120th frame, one file
overwritten) is unchanged. The legacy vtable path is not covered.

Why: one overwritten dump cannot show how a title's screen changes over a
long unattended run, and a black frame cannot tell "cleared to black" from
"nothing drawn". Gran Turismo 6's first frame under the port is all black;
the counts beside each numbered frame answer which.

Test: tools/test_frame_series.py (new; builds libs/video/tests/
test_frame_series.c for the policy, names, caps, stop file and the PPM and
stats writers, and on macOS libs/video/tests/test_metal_frame_series.m for
the backend's present glue against a real Metal texture), and
libs/video/tests/test_rsx_draw_engine.c gains test_frame_counts
(tools/test_rsx_immediate_vertices.py).

